
usage: colliding_pixels_generator.py [-h] --a X Y --b X Y --mirror-a MX MY --mirror-b MX MY --time MS 
       [--width WIDTH] [--height HEIGHT] [--window MS] [--clearance PX] [--top N] [--check X Y]



Example:   python3 colliding_pixels_curves.py --a 0 15 --target-a 29 15 --duration-a 3000 --sine-a 14 2 --b 15 0 --target-b 15 29 --duration-b 3000 --sine-b 10 3

Generates two pixels, both using a sinewave path.  The first pixel starts at 0,15 and heads toward 29,15.  The second starts at 15,0 and head toward 15,29.  
The amplitude of the sinewave for pixelA is 14 and will traverse 2 cycles in 3000ms.  The amplitude for pixelB is 10 and will traverse 3 cycles in 3000ms..

